<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Howard Smith year net up 11.8 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Howard Smith year net up 11.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		   132.19 vs 118.06</p>
<p>    Net profit			    86.13 vs  77.06</p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)	     19.0 vs 17.5</p>
<p>NOTE: Howard Smith Ltd  SMI AX is a shipping, engineering and hardware group.  </p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)		 34.0 vs 32.5</p>
<p>    Sales (billion)			  2.10 vs 2.19</p>
<p>    Other income			    62.63 vs 29.99</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)				45.8 vs 44.4</p>
<p>    Abnormal profit (before tax)	 3.48 vs 4.63</p>
<p>Dividend is 100 percent franked</p>
<p>Pay date Oct 4</p>
<p>Reg date Oct 1</p>
<p>    Tax					 49.54 vs  41.53</p>
<p>    Interest				  35.34 vs  37.29</p>
<p>    Depreciation			    57.69 vs  60.92</p>
<p>NOTE: Howard Smith said the abnormals reflected profit from sale of shipping business, which was partially offset by redundancy costs.</p>
<p>Industry segments - profit before tax</p>
<p>    Shipping				  23.30 vs 11.15</p>
<p>    Towage and agency		     30.52 vs 32.27</p>
<p>    Engineering			     19.70 vs 15.27</p>
<p>    Distribution - Industrial	   48.77 vs 44.45</p>
<p>    Distribution - Hardware	     50.35 vs 55.83</p>
<p>    Investment and Corporate	loss 7.45 vs loss 7.65</p>
<p>    Other activities			  nil vs  0.83</p>
</text>
